BSDMemory test coverage
=======================

pressure_test exercises watermark boundaries, immediate escalation, three-sample
recovery, and retention of the last valid restriction across unknown samples.

dependency_test calls the daemon's actual sampling/publication helpers with
injected clients. It checks failure errno across cleanup, counter length
validation, missing notification state, unchanged-state suppression and
republication after reconnect.

startup_test calls the daemon's actual main function. Provider operations,
kqueue/timer events, dependency clients and the sampling clock are injected.
The fixture checks all startup failure points, readiness after timer setup,
resource release before quiescence acknowledgement, retry timing, uninterrupted
heartbeats through dependency failures, and three valid samples before pressure
recovery. Each RPC stub checks that a real libservice budget is active. The
heartbeat failure case starts with both clients live and checks their cleanup,
provider destruction, failure exit status and removal of the active RPC budget.
The timer advances virtual time; these are not wall-clock latency measurements.
Queue cleanup uses a real descriptor standing in for the event queue.

Remaining full-system checks include actual SwitchBoard readiness/stop RPCs,
capability-mode queue creation, real BSDSysctl/BSDNotify stalls and restarts,
pressure delivery to caches, and low-memory/OOM survivability. These fixtures
do not reserve memory, activate the bundle, or exercise the kernel OOM selector.
